From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0530: resolve_dual_write_msaa (MSAA and offset/partial destinations), resolve_defer_memory_write (deferred, materialised on demand), clear_full_resource, resolve_dual_write_nomem_dev

Source: Ours (stream LOCK60 wave 2, F2). Validated in game: runs lk-fl2 (verify), lk-fl3, lk-fl4, lk-fl5, lk-fl6, lk-val2
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: D3D12. Four levers of the resolve/clear floor, one patch because they share functions:
  resolve_dual_write_msaa (false; PC profile true): 0490's dual write also for 2x/4x sources and for resolves into a sub-rectangle
    of a texture (shadow cascades into the atlas; origin in xe_resolve_dual_info bits 4..31; 8 new *_dual_origin DXBC, fxc
    10.0.26100, the 60 existing resolve shaders rebuild 'same'); partial writes keep a texture up to date only if it was before.
    resolve_dual_write_verify covers msaa and partial: 0 bytes differ (lk-fl2). Scene -0.33 ms (lk-fl6, with the two below).
  resolve_defer_memory_write (false): a full-cover colour dual write skips its shared-memory store (null UAV) and records it;
    materialised from the texture (resolve_materialize_{32,64}bpp) when any consumer requests the bytes (RequestRanges hook,
    readback, texture writes, cache clear, verify); dropped when a later resolve rewrites every tile; tile-exact exclusions for
    partial overwrites; adaptive back-off (resolve_defer_backoff_frames 300) for destinations that keep getting materialised.
    _poison / _verify proof modes clean (lk-fl4/5). Net -0.09 ms (lk-fl6): stays off.
  clear_full_resource / _pad / _poison (false): NumRects=0 clears where the outside is dead; strict qualifies ~nothing, pad
    (unprovable) measured +0.26 ms SLOWER (lk-fl4): stays off.
  resolve_dual_write_nomem_dev (false): DEVELOPMENT MEASUREMENT, NOT EXACT (memory stores discarded): -1.07 ms (lk-fl2).
Bucket: REDO

0530-resolve-dual-write-msaa-defer-clears.patch (mcla-x86 LOCK60 wave 2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
index 06a30662..da412d35 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
@@ -82,6 +82,30 @@ class D3D12CommandProcessor : public CommandProcessor {
 
   uint64_t GetCurrentSubmission() const { return submission_current_; }
   uint64_t GetCompletedSubmission() const { return submission_completed_; }
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0560): resolve_defer_memory_write: whether commands can be recorded now
+  // (GetDeferredCommandList), and whether every resolve is read back to the guest memory (the
+  // global readback mode: its resolves are not deferred; the ones a rule of readback_resolve_rules
+  // matches are materialised before they're copied).
+  bool IsSubmissionOpen() const { return submission_open_; }
+  bool IsReadbackResolveGloballyEnabled() const;
+  // The pipeline last bound, to bind it again after a compute dispatch made in the middle of
+  // something that has bound its own pipeline (a draw's requests of the shared memory, which
+  // make the bytes of a deferred resolve write: SetExternalPipeline would leave the compute
+  // pipeline set for the draw). At most one of them is set.
+  struct PipelineBinding {
+    void* guest = nullptr;
+    ID3D12PipelineState* external = nullptr;
+  };
+  PipelineBinding GetPipelineBinding() const {
+    PipelineBinding binding;
+    binding.guest = current_guest_pipeline_;
+    binding.external = current_external_pipeline_;
+    return binding;
+  }
+  void RestorePipelineBinding(const PipelineBinding& binding);
+  // The vertex buffers requested earlier in the frame that overlap the range are requested again
+  // by the draws that use them (a deferred resolve write makes a range's bytes stale).
+  void InvalidateVertexBufferResidencyForRange(uint32_t start, uint32_t length);
 
   // Must be called when a subsystem does something like UpdateTileMappings so
   // it can be awaited in CheckSubmissionFence(submission_current_) if it was
